{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-27T08:25:47.049Z","data":{"text":"Task complete. Summary:\n\n**Added `src/core/status/inbox-sound.ts`** — `createInboxSound(projectRoot, config, deps)` returning `{ notify(now) }`, plus exported `InboxSound`, `InboxSoundDeps`, and `InboxSoundChild` types. It resolves the sound/player once: `off`/`bell`/`default` (`PACKAGE_ROOT/sounds/inbox.wav`)/project-relative path; darwin `afplay`, linux first of `pw-play`/`paplay`/`aplay` found as executable files in `PATH`; warns once through `warn` on a missing file; spawns detached with ignored output and rings on error/throw; honors local quiet hours (start inclusive, end exclusive, cross-midnight) and the `soundWindowSeconds` window.\n\n**Added `tests/inbox-sound.test.ts`** — 13 tests with recording seams and fake executables in a temp dir, covering every \"Inbox sound\" scenario including the watcher/harness import scan. No test makes a sound.\n\n**Verification**\n- `node --import tsx --test tests/inbox-sound.test.ts` → 13/13 pass\n- `pnpm verify` → EXIT=0 (typechecks, build, full suite, lint)\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/098-inbox-follow-sound/.run/results/3.md`. Only the two scoped files plus the result file were touched. The one ambiguity I flagged: `<path>` in the missing-file warning is the resolved absolute path."}}
